---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
const updated = "Last updated: October 31, 2026";
---

<Base
	title="Privacy Policy — ame_dev"
	description="How ame_dev handles personal information and user data across its website and apps."
	lang="en"
	alt={{ ja: "/privacy/", zh: "/zh/privacy/" }}
>
	<article class="legal">
		<div class="container container--narrow">
			<span class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</span>
			<h1 class="legal__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p class="legal__updated">{updated}</p>

			<p>
				ame_dev ("we") sets out below how personal information and user data are handled on the
				website and in the applications we provide (the "Services").
			</p>

			<h2>1. About this website</h2>
			<p>
				If you contact us by email, the content of your message and your contact details are
				used solely to reply and respond to your inquiry.
			</p>

			<h3>Analytics (Google Analytics)</h3>
			<p>
				To improve this website, we use Google Analytics, an analytics tool provided by Google LLC,
				only if you allow it. Only when you choose "Allow" in the prompt shown on your first visit are
				cookies stored on your device and information such as the pages you view, time spent, the type
				of device and browser you use, and your approximate region sent to Google. We do not collect
				information that identifies you, such as your name or email address.
			</p>
			<ul class="legal__list">
				<li>If you choose "Decline", no Google Analytics cookies are stored and no information is sent.</li>
				<li>You can change your choice at any time from "Cookie settings" at the bottom of each page.</li>
				<li>The information collected is managed by Google in accordance with Google's privacy policy. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a> for details.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>2. About the Drive DAM app</h2>
			<p>
				Drive DAM runs entirely on your PC. We do not collect your images, files, tags, notes, or
				any other data through Drive DAM, nor do we transmit them to external servers.
			</p>
			<ul class="legal__list">
				<li>Your image files remain in the shared folders you designate and are never sent to us.</li>
				<li>Tags, colors, favorites, notes, and similar information are stored in the same folder as your images (<code>_dam/</code>) and are shared only within your team.</li>
				<li>Synchronization with storage services such as Google Drive, Dropbox, or Box is performed by the service you have installed, and the privacy policy of that service applies.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Additionally, Drive DAM performs the following internal operations.
			</p>
			<ul class="legal__list">
				<li>To identify edit history, an internal identifier is automatically generated per device. This identifier is not sent to us; it is used solely within the shared folder to distinguish who made which edits.</li>
				<li>If Drive DAM was obtained from the Microsoft Store, the Microsoft Store license API is used to check trial expiration and process purchases. Information accessed through this API is managed by Microsoft's account infrastructure and is not transmitted to us.</li>
				<li>Settings and thumbnail caches are stored on your PC (under <code>%APPDATA%</code> and <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%</code>).</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>3. About the Tsumist app</h2>
			<p>
				Tsumist runs entirely on your PC. We do not collect your tasks, notes, or any other data
				through Tsumist, nor do we transmit them to external servers. No account registration is
				required to use the app.
			</p>
			<ul class="legal__list">
				<li>Tasks, categories, history, settings, and similar data are stored only on your PC (under <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%</code>).</li>
				<li>Images you set as a board background are likewise stored on your PC and are never sent to us.</li>
				<li>The app does not require an internet connection to use its features.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Additionally, Tsumist performs the following internal operations.
			</p>
			<ul class="legal__list">
				<li>If Tsumist was obtained from the Microsoft Store, the Microsoft Store license API is used to check the purchase status of the add-on and to process purchases. Information accessed through this API is managed by Microsoft's account infrastructure and is not transmitted to us.</li>
				<li>If you use the paid edition purchased on BOOTH, that information is recorded only on your PC.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>4. Disclosure to third parties</h2>
			<p>
				We do not provide users' personal information to third parties, except where required by law.
			</p>

			<h2>5. Changes to this policy</h2>
			<p>
				This policy may be revised as needed. Any changes take effect once posted on this page.
			</p>

			<h2>6. Contact</h2>
			<p>
				For inquiries about the Services or this policy, please contact
				<a href="mailto:amemitai@gmail.com">amemitai@gmail.com</a>.
			</p>

			<p class="legal__back"><a href="/en/drivedam/">← Back to Drive DAM</a></p>
		</div>
	</article>
</Base>

<style>
	.legal {
		padding-block: 72px 88px;
	}
	.container--narrow {
		max-width: var(--maxw-narrow);
	}
	.legal__title {
		font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 1.2rem + 1.6vw, 2.2rem);
		margin-bottom: 10px;
	}
	.legal__updated {
		color: var(--ink-faint);
		font-size: 0.88rem;
		margin-bottom: 36px;
	}
	.legal p {
		color: var(--ink-muted);
		margin-bottom: 18px;
		line-height: 1.95;
	}
	.legal h2 {
		font-size: 1.2rem;
		margin-top: 38px;
		margin-bottom: 14px;
		padding-top: 8px;
	}
	.legal h3 {
		font-size: 1rem;
		margin-top: 26px;
		margin-bottom: 10px;
	}
	.legal__list {
		color: var(--ink-muted);
		line-height: 1.9;
		padding-left: 1.3em;
		margin-bottom: 18px;
	}
	.legal__list li {
		margin-bottom: 10px;
	}
	.legal__back {
		margin-top: 48px;
		padding-top: 24px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
	}
</style>
